q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $-1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))$ at $x=0.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252816 1113 #uuid "6d72eb11-db3f-5e0d-9fd0-7dd743dc99d6" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252816 1145 "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))=3{q}^{′}(x)+4{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3q(x)+4r(x))|}_{x=0} & =3{q}^{′}(0)+4{r}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =3(2)+4(-1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252817 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252818 13194139533809 true] [17592186252817 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533809 true] [17592186252817 1041 "field-1" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252817 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252818 13194139533809 true] [17592186252817 1110 #uuid "a537318f-83e9-5874-add3-56b0f3be2afe" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252818 1034 "2" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252818 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533809 true] [17592186252818 1111 #uuid "8ee2f22c-0ceb-5f3b-8f8e-ebb97c7f902c" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252819 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252820 13194139533809 true] [17592186252819 1089 "q-48843" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252819 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533809 true] [17592186252819 1100 "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(1)=8,\\,{f}^{′}(1)=6,\\,g(1)=4,\\,{g}^{′}(1)=4\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=1.$" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252819 1113 #uuid "1eda30ce-5b87-5095-9f12-acc78818a070" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252819 1145 "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=1} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(1)g(1)-f(1){g}^{′}(1)}{{g}^{2}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 4-8\\cdot 4}{{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252821 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252822 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252823 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252824 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252825 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1041 "selection" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252821 13194139533809 true] [17592186252820 1110 #uuid "4d6db62a-956d-58f8-a39a-b5dc6f46dfd4" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252821 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252821 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533809 true] [17592186252821 1111 #uuid "c090bbc8-1fc5-51ca-a64e-44459e5d75cf" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252822 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252822 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533809 true] [17592186252822 1111 #uuid "44d9749a-31f1-5939-a2e2-d94ed7d8f6f8" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252823 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252823 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533809 true] [17592186252823 1111 #uuid "5d6e3d1d-f3c8-5548-9722-375ba8f89b37" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252824 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252824 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533809 true] [17592186252824 1111 #uuid "684a73d4-8f0d-508e-9e1d-0b590a2fc205" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252825 1034 "-2" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252825 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533809 true] [17592186252825 1111 #uuid "90de668c-0bc5-5468-be40-97037977efe1" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252826 1017 #edb/ref 17592186252827 13194139533809 true] [17592186252826 1089 "q-48965" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252826 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533809 true] [17592186252826 1100 "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(2)=-1,\\,{f}^{′}(2)=-2,\\,g(2)=-5,\\,{g}^{′}(2)=1\n$$\n\nIf $h(x)=\\frac{5f(x)+4}{g(x)+6},$ find the value of ${h}^{′}(2).$" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252826 1113 #uuid "18e1de8e-0324-5cfc-8ed1-bb965f60a808" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252826 1145 "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=5f(x)+4$ and $v=g(x)+6.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{v{u}^{′}-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(g(x)+6)\\cdot 5{f}^{′}(x)-(5f(x)+4)\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x)+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{f}^{′}(x)(g(x)+6)-{g}^{′}(x)(5f(x)+4)}{(g(x)+6)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{5{f}^{′}(2)(g(2)+6)-{g}^{′}(2)(5f(2)+4)}{(g(2)+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-5+6)-1\\cdot (5\\cdot (-1)+4)}{(-5+6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-10)\\cdot 1-(-1)}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252828 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252829 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252830 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252831 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252832 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1041 "selection" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252828 13194139533809 true] [17592186252827 1110 #uuid "74eac84e-7d80-54a7-9ac7-d2f58632c75a" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252828 1034 "-9" 13194139533809 true] [17592186252828 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604545